  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Executive Seminar 01-25: &quot;Climate Change and Security&quot;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. These flagship courses seek to stimulate dialogue on strategic issues affecting the Near East South Asia region among national security professionals. Topics include U.S. foreign policy; the current and future regional strategic issues; counterterrorism; the proliferation of weapons of mass destruction, and disaster management. 2. These courses are conducted three times a year: 1st, 3rd, and 4th Quarters.</narrative>
  </description>
